{title: The God of Abraham Praise}
{artist: Thomas Olivers}
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
The [Em]God of Abraham [Am]praise, who [B]reigns en[Em]throned above —
[G]Ancient of ever[Am]lasting [B]days and [Em]God of [B]love.
Je[Em]hovah, great I [Am]AM, by [B]earth and [Em]heaven confessed,
[G]I bow and bless the [Am]sacred [B]name for[Em]ever [B]blessed.

Verse 2
The God of Abr'ham praise,
at Whose supreme command
From earth I rise and seek the joys at His
right hand; I all on earth forsake,
its wisdom,
fame, and pow'r;
And Him my only Portion
make, my
Shield and Tow'r.

Verse 3
The God of Abr'ham praise,
Whose all sufficient grace
Shall guide me all my happy days, in all
my ways. He calls a worm His friend,
He calls
Himself my God!
And He shall save me to the
end, thro'
Jesus' blood.

Verse 4
He by Himself has sworn;
I on His oath depend,
I shall, on eagle wings upborne, to Heav'n
ascend. I shall behold His face;
I shall
His pow'r adore,
And sing the wonders of His
grace forevermore.

Verse 5
Tho' nature's strength decay,
and earth and hell withstand,
To Canaan's bounds I urge my way, at His
command. The wat'ry deep I pass,
with Jesus
in my view;
And thro' the howling wilderness my
way pursue.
